  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner who became famous for completing marathons in a bionic suit after being paralyzed in a 2007 horse riding accident, has died following an accident in Jordan on August 22. Lomas, who was paralyzed from the chest down after breaking her neck, back, and ribs at the Osberton Horse Trials, raised nearly £1 million for charity through various events. She gained national attention for completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days using a bionic suit and was honored by lighting the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square. In 2016, she completed the Great North Run in five days while pregnant, again wearing her bionic suit. Her family has requested privacy as they grieve her loss."
